  "answer": "The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Changes to `pagination.mjs`\n\nI replaced the buggy implementation with a correct one. The original had three bugs:\n- Used `page * pageSize` as the start index (wrong for 1-based pages).\n- Used `Math.floor` instead of `Math.ceil` for `totalPages`.\n- Always returned `page + 1` for `nextPage`, even on the last page.\n\n## New behavior\n\n- **Validation**: Throws `TypeError` if `items` isn't an array; throws `RangeError` if `page` or `pageSize` isn't a positive safe integer (using `Number.isSafeInteger`).\n- **1-based pages**: Start index is `(page - 1) * pageSize`.\n- **`totalPages`**: `Math.ceil(items.length / pageSize)`.\n- **`nextPage`**: `page + 1` only when `page < totalPages`, otherwise `null`.\n- **Empty input**: `totalPages` is `0`, `items` is `[]`, `nextPage` is `null`.\n- **Page beyond last**: `items` is `[]`, `nextPage` is `null`, and `totalPages` still reflects the real count.\n- **No mutation**: `slice` returns a new array and elements are untouched.\n- **Named export** `paginate` is preserved.\n\nThe two provided tests (`first page uses 1-based numbering` and `last page has no successor`) now pass with this logic.",
